{"causes": ["The powerful House of Horne's influence helped secure Arnold's initial ecclesiastical appointments.", "The ongoing political fragmentation and urban unrest within the Prince-Bishopric of Liège necessitated strong, albeit often contested, leadership.", "The Western Schism (1378–1417) created a complex web of allegiances and rivalries that directly impacted Arnold's ability to govern and maintain stability."], "effects": ["Arnold II's rule contributed to the escalation of long-standing conflicts, such as the War of the Awans and the Warous, within the Liège nobility.", "His struggles against urban communes, particularly the Liège revolt of 1384, reinforced the growing power and assertiveness of the cities against episcopal authority.", "His death left the Prince-Bishopric of Liège in a state of continued political instability and unresolved internal tensions."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "western-schism", "sourceName": "Western Schism", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "arnold-ii-of-horne", "targetName": "Arnold II of Horne", "context": "The Western Schism profoundly influenced Arnold II's political decisions and allegiances as Prince-Bishop of Liège from 1378 to 1389."}, {"sourceSlug": "arnold-ii-of-horne", "sourceName": "Arnold II of Horne", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "liege-prince-bishopric", "targetName": "Prince-Bishopric of Liège", "context": "Arnold II of Horne's most significant period of rule, from 1378 until his death in 1389, occurred within the Prince-Bishopric of Liège."}, {"sourceSlug": "arnold-ii-of-horne", "sourceName": "Arnold II of Horne", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "war-of-the-awans-and-the-warous", "targetName": "War of the Awans and the Warous", "context": "Arnold II of Horne inherited and actively participated in the complex noble feud known as the War of the Awans and the Warous during his time in Liège."}, {"sourceSlug": "john-of-arkel", "sourceName": "John of Arkel", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug"